<title>GERMANY: Bayer sells cold product brandname to Merck.</title>
<headline>Bayer sells cold product brandname to Merck.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Bayer AG said on Wednesday that it plans to sell its trademark name Larylin to German drugs group Merck KGaA by the end of the year.</p>
<p>Bayer said had reached agreement to sell the brandname, which encompasses 11 different cold remedies sold without prescriptions at pharmacies, to Merck by January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The price was not disclosed but Bayer said the move would not involve any job cuts.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
